                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26cbe7d9-5d43-3935-8e7a-3a3ffb756328",
                        "entry_id": "b4ff97ba-fb48-3be8-b227-400af8d1d78d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to pronounce an unstressed о like an а (as seen in Central and Southern Russia, considered standard)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10027f9a-d4d7-4d2b-95d2-d4f33827f41d",
                                "sense_id": "26cbe7d9-5d43-3935-8e7a-3a3ffb756328",
                                "text": "Москвичи́ а́кают.",
                                "translation": "Muscovites pronounce unstressed o's like a's.",
                                "english": "Muscovites pronounce unstressed o's like a's."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b84acb5-4025-4d82-8292-ad3159b97844",
                                "sense_id": "26cbe7d9-5d43-3935-8e7a-3a3ffb756328",
                                "text": "Учи́тель отме́тил, что произноше́ние на́ше ужа́сно, заста́вил а́кать по-моско́вски и петербу́ргски: каро́ва, пашёл, маладо́й, вада́.",
                                "translation": "The teacher noted that our pronunciation was horrible and he made us say words in the Moscow and St. Petersburg way: karóva, pašól, maladój, vadá. [i.e., words with an unstressed о (o): коро́ва (koróva), пошёл (pošól), молодо́й (molodój), вода́ (vodá)]",
                                "english": "The teacher noted that our pronunciation was horrible and he made us say words in the Moscow and St. Petersburg way: karóva, pašól, maladój, vadá. [i.e., words with an unstressed о (o): коро́ва (koróva), пошёл (pošól), молодо́й (molodój), вода́ (vodá)]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
